  "query_preview": "/Monday through Friday/...\nThrough the week, a high amplitude trough will become a cut off\nlow in southern California and linger in the Great Basin. As \nthe trough builds along the West Coast Monday evening, \nincreasing clouds and breezy conditions in SE Oregon are \nexpected. Residual dry conditions with the wind will support \nelevated fire weather, though impacts will be minimal as the low \ncontinues to move in. Temperatures will cool off Tuesday as a \nfront moves through, cooling temperatures down to near-normal; \nlow-mid 60s for the afternoon high in lower elevations, low 50s \nfor mountain valleys. Ensemble guidance largely favors another \ncold front on Thursday as the low moves weakens and rejoins the \nbroader flow. This will lead to even cold temperatures, about 5 \ndegrees below normal, Thursday and Friday. Colder temps are \naccompanied by the best chances for precipitation across much of\nthe area, with valley rain and mountain snow possible.",
